---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description={`${SITE.name} is a ${SITE.descriptor.toLowerCase()}, graduating ${SITE.gradYear}.`}
>
  <header class="head">
    <div class="prose-wrap">
      <h1>About</h1>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="prose-wrap body">
    {/*
      Kevin: this page is deliberately short and factual, because everything here
      is something you confirmed. Expand it in your own voice — the things a
      reader cannot get from the project pages are the ones worth adding:

        - how you got into robotics, and how that led into graphics
        - why you kept building engines instead of using libraries
        - what you want to work on at Purdue, and after
        - anything outside engineering that matters to you

      Keep it honest and specific. Do not add coursework, GPA, awards, or
      positions that are not real — the project pages carry the proof and this
      page only has to carry you.
    */}

    <p class="lede">
      I&rsquo;m a computer science undergraduate at Purdue, graduating in {SITE.gradYear},
      and most of what I build starts by working out the mathematics underneath it.
    </p>

    <p>
      That began with games and simulations written in an environment with no
      graphics, physics, or interface libraries available, so anything I wanted had
      to be built: projection, collision, parsing, animation. It carried into
      competition robotics with FIRST Tech Challenge, where the same instinct
      applies to autonomous navigation and control, and more recently into a
      computer-vision research project.
    </p>

    <h2>Where to find me</h2>

    <ul class="links">
      <li>
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>
          <Icon name="mail" size={18} />
          <span>{SITE.email}</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={SITE.github} rel="me noopener">
          <Icon name="github" size={18} />
          <span>github.com/kc0817</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={SITE.linkedin} rel="me noopener">
          <Icon name="linkedin" size={18} />
          <span>LinkedIn</span>
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>

    {
      !SITE.resume && (
        <p class="pending">
          A current résumé is on its way onto this page.
        </p>
      )
    }
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .head {
    padding-block: var(--section-y) var(--s-6);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: var(--ground-sunken);
  }

  .head h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.038em;
  }

  .body {
    padding-block: var(--s-8) var(--section-y);
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-tight);
    line-height: 1.42;
    margin-bottom: var(--s-5);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--accent-orange);
    padding-top: var(--s-5);
  }

  .body p {
    color: var(--ink-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--s-4);
  }

  .lede {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .body h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-top: var(--s-8);
    margin-bottom: var(--s-4);
  }

  .links {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-3);
  }

  .links a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .links a span {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--rule-strong);
    text-underline-offset: 0.24em;
    transition: text-decoration-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .links a:hover span {
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent-orange-deep);
  }

  .links svg {
    color: var(--ink-tertiary);
    flex: none;
  }

  .pending {
    margin-top: var(--s-7);
    padding-top: var(--s-5);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--ink-tertiary);
  }
</style>
